"# aos-tree-start: start the root of a tree, refusing another tree's environment\n\nIt checks the environment, then becomes `aos-exec` with the same arguments, in the foreground (same pid; Ctrl-C stops the whole tree). For the usual tree `aos-tree-start root` is `aos-exec root`. Use it instead of `aos-exec` when you start a new tree.\n\n```sh\nsource ~/repo/aos/proto8/env.sh && cd ~/aos-home && aos-tree-start root\naos-tree-start -- --stack stacks/root defs      # aos-exec arguments that start with - go after --\n```\n\nWhat it checks: any `AOS_*` variable other than `AOS_HOME` (`AOS_STACK`, `AOS_DAEMON`, `AOS_WS` ...) means this shell was started by another tree or by an agent in one, and the new root would take that tree's stack or daemon as its own. Then it refuses:\n\n```text\naos-tree-start: error: EnvBad AOS_DAEMON, AOS_STACK set in this shell (inherited from another tree or an agent's shell?): the root would use them; clear every AOS_* except AOS_HOME first (source PROTO8/env.sh, in bash), or pass --force\n```\n\nIt names the variables, never their values. `proto8/env.sh` clears every `AOS_*`, sets `AOS_HOME` to that proto8 and puts its `bin/` (first), `cmd/*/bin` and `frontend/bin` first on `PATH` (`bin/` is filled by `python3 install.py`); from an agent's shell source it with bash, not zsh.\n\n- If you are an agent, your shell carries these variables, so expect `EnvBad`. The way past it is `env.sh` (in bash), not `--force`.\n- `--force` is for starting a tree inside a tree on purpose (tests). It starts anyway and prints one line `aos-tree-start: warning: starting with inherited ... (--force)`. It must come before the first argument: after it, every word is handed to aos-exec as it is.\n- No argument = `ArgumentsBad`; it does not fill in `root` for you.\n- Plain `aos-exec root` is not checked: only this command knows that a new tree is being started.\n\nIt prints nothing itself when the check passes. Exit code: whatever aos-exec returns; 1 for its own errors on stderr: `EnvBad`, `ArgumentsBad`, `CommandMissing` (aos-exec is not on PATH; source `proto8/env.sh` first), `FlagUnknown`.\n"
